{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"Sibling of bugs 3d57-602f-0b75-48ee and a3f5-5c19-faad-417b (found in a3f5's Step-7 construct sweep): the delivered-children manifest pays a full-store scan per child during Pass-2 completion sub-call assembly.\n\n## Mechanism\n\norchestrator.delivered_children_manifest (src/rebar/llm/plan_review/orchestrator.py) loops a container's children and calls attest.delivered_now -> _attested_delivered -> compute_validity(sig, child, 'completion-verifier') per closed child; the completion branch recomputes current_material_fingerprint (1 full-store reduce via relation_snapshot.live_material_children), a stale fingerprint retries 3 legacy generations (_legacy_material_ok), and explain_material_change enumerates once more — O(5N) full-store scans per manifest assembly (measured: 6 scans for 1 child, 21 for 4). a3f5's fix wrapped only completion_child_gate; this call path reaches the fingerprints OUTSIDE any snapshot (verified RED on main containing 37d29f017c88).\n\n## Fix\n\nSame remedy shape as 3d57 (14aa285f963) and a3f5 (37d29f017c88): open `with material_child_index(repo_root=repo_root):` around the delivered_now loop in delivered_children_manifest. One wide scan per assembly instead of O(5N); both snapshot and slow paths filter through counts_as_plan_material_child, so manifest membership is unchanged.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Full-store reduce count during delivered_children_manifest does not grow with child count — proven by `python -m pytest tests/unit/test_delivered_manifest_scan_count.py::test_delivered_manifest_scan_count_constant_in_child_count` (RED before the fix: 6 vs 21 scans; GREEN after).\n- [ ] Delivered manifest membership unchanged: a child attesting its true current fingerprint appears in the manifest, a stale child does not — proven by `python -m pytest tests/unit/test_delivered_manifest_scan_count.py` (correctness guard).\n- [ ] `make lint` + `make typecheck` + complexity ratchet (`python scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py --check`) clean.\n\n## Testing\n\nRED-first counting-seam regression test tests/unit/test_delivered_manifest_scan_count.py (mirrors tests/unit/test_completion_child_gate_scan_count.py): monkeypatch-counts rebar._engine_support.reads.reduce_all_tickets, asserts scan count constant in child count, plus manifest-membership correctness guard. Mutation check: fix reverted returns the test to RED. Neighbor suites green (test_delivered_now, test_completion_floor, test_completion_floor_e2e, test_completion_child_gate_scan_count)."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787453302635593001,"uuid":"e57f3fef-08c1-4207-876e-0b5e45fa209a"}